+# Visual options and references
+
+Read for explore, specify, and architect when a choice is easier to judge visually or content
+has flow, sequence, state, or component relationships, and for implement and review when the
+owning record links a visual reference. Paths under
+`docs/lusona/` are in the consuming project.
+
+## When
+
+- Offer 2-4 visual options when a concept, architecture, or UI choice is better judged by
+  seeing it than by reading a description. Do not offer options during implement when the
+  agreement already settles the choice.
+- Include an explanatory diagram whenever content has flow, sequence, state, or component
+  relationships. Purely textual decisions get none.
+
+## Presentation
+
+- Show a simple diagram inline in the reply as Unicode or ASCII text.
+- Write a larger diagram or a UI mockup as a standalone HTML file. For Mermaid, put the source in
+  `<pre class="mermaid">` and load a pinned script, such as
+  `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11.4.1/dist/mermaid.min.js`; the source stays readable
+  when the script cannot load. Rendering requires no specific host.
+- Open the file in the browser when the host permits; otherwise report its absolute path.
+- Write draft options outside tracked records: in a scratch directory the host provides for the
+  session, or in the project's ignored temporary directory.
+
+## Choice
+
+Label options A, B, C, D. Ask the user to choose by letter through the native question tool
+under [Questions and next actions](../README.md#questions-and-next-actions), otherwise in plain
+text. There is no click-capture server. If the user rejects all options or asks for revision,
+save nothing and offer revised options.
+
+## Retention after a choice
+
+Save only after the user chooses, and only within the core write authority and no-save
+restrictions; otherwise report the reference in the response.
+
+- Directory: `docs/lusona/visuals/<record-id>/`, where `<record-id>` is the owning spec or ADR
+  basename, or the notes slug when no spec exists yet.
+- Save the chosen visual as a static file: the HTML mockup, or Mermaid in a Markdown file.
+- Create `reference.md` from the [visual reference template](../templates/visual-reference.md):
+  chosen option, who chose it and when, visual link, owner link, binding items, illustrative
+  items, and one line per rejected option with the reason.
+- Binding items (IDs V1, V2, ...) default to layout regions, element order, which controls exist,
+  and information hierarchy. Illustrative items default to colors, copy, and spacing unless the
+  user marks them binding.
+- Do not save rejected option files.
+- Link `reference.md` from the owning spec, ADR, or notes.
+
+A user-supplied reference keeps its existing capture in specify. Retain it this way only when
+the user asks.
+
+## Consumption
+
+- Implement treats each binding item as acceptance input and reports each item's status in its
+  result. Illustrative items are not acceptance.
+- Review checks each binding item against the result and reports it as met, unmet, or unchecked.
+  Without a screenshot tool, check against code or markup, report the visual comparison as unrun,
+  and state that human visual acceptance remains required.
+- A record without a visual reference leaves implement and review unchanged.
